                    <pre class="azure-notes-text">Creating Azure Virtual machine in Azure Portal

Step 1: Login into the Microsoft Azure Portal.




Step 2: Click on Create Virtual Machine as shown in the figure below.




Step 3: Know and configure the requirements according to the needs like subscription type,
in which region you want to create your virtual machine, and the availability zone and type
of image(OS flavor) and key-pait to connect ot the virtual machine with the git bash or putty.
Step 4: In this step, you need to configure the type od os disk you want like the type and the
size of the disk etc.




Step 5: Select the network in which you want to configure your virtual machine and you can
control the inbound and outbound of the virtual machine with the help of the network.
After configuring all the requirements know click on Review+Create.</pre>
